This proved the dedicated vehicle catalog reached Unreal's skeletal presentation
boundary without flattening the vehicle into a static-mesh transaction. At that
stage, the broader native construction boundary still lacked the reviewed
Physics Asset, materials, wheel definitions, and Chaos composition.

The native `SharVehicles` automation run at that stage passed all three then-
registered tests with zero test warnings or errors. Definition validation,
damage runtime, and selection were green, while native vehicle construction had
not yet been implemented. That result narrowed the next P0 step to the typed
construction boundary rather than another catalog or skeletal-import repair.

The typed native presentation boundary now exists without changing the
identity/tuning contract in `USharVehicleDefinition`.
`USharVehiclePresentationDefinition` requires the final Skeletal Mesh, Skeleton,
Physics Asset, Animation Blueprint class, ordered Material Instances, semantic
rig profile, deterministic preparation revision, and ordered wheel bindings.
Each wheel binding carries its canonical wheel id, exact skeletal bone, and
native Chaos wheel class. The project registers this definition as the
`SharVehiclePresentation` Primary Asset type, and `SharVehicles` now declares
the `ChaosVehicles` module while the project explicitly enables
`ChaosVehiclesPlugin`.

