The same inspection exposed a distinct presentation defect. Source headlight
assets are camera-facing billboard groups attached to `hll` and `hlr`, but the
current FBX representation leaves their cards as fixed planes, so they can
vanish when viewed from the back. Two disposable native SpotLight actors were
placed at the source-derived `hll`/`hlr` rest positions for visual comparison;
they are inspection-only and the level is not an authority or persistence
surface. Production still requires a native vehicle-light adapter plus reviewed
camera-facing glow presentation rather than a two-sided-material approximation.

